  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-11-06T14:10:29.789Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It'd be great to have a simple, native solution for footstep sounds in worlds. Basically a system that plays from randomized arrays of footstep sounds and can account for avatar gait, pace, height + world ground types. \n\nThere are \"workaround\" methods to pull a simple version of this within worlds already with the best known method heavily using Standard Assets, UI buttons, Animators, and triggers to get a player's state + play one shots locally. It's somewhat complicated, and the complexity can increase exponentially if you want to do something like swap sounds for different ground types. It's also not (sensibly) ideal to give OTHER players footsteps with these methods [which is more important for immersion!](https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2018/09/180912133507.htm)\n\nA possible implementation might be a 'VRC_AudioMaterial' component that you put on game objects to dictate their audio properties. This component could be a general audio material utility for footstep surface type, PhysSound, and audio propagation properties (absorption / scattering / transmission) in the future.",
